 all the claims that are made  about you but these guys want to work  with you when i first started my  software company  we had a hard time getting started we  had a hard time bringing on customers i  felt like  felt like things should be moving faster  i felt like we had great talent and  skill a great product why is this taking  so long you know i was pulling out 300  bucks a month  at the start 300 bucks it wasn't enough  to survive and it got so  frustrating  and i thought there has to be a faster  way there has to be an easier way like  this should not be so hard i write the  book saw the videos all about  entrepreneurship it looks so easy and  yet i'm i'm the stupid one who can't  figure this thing out  and i looked at companies like microsoft  and how they got started and it was  through partnerships  they partnered up their big deal was  with when they partnered with ibm and  they said every ibm that goes out has  microsoft software on it so instead of  selling to consumers one at a time at a  time at a time at a time they partnered  up with one company who was able to sell  tons of software for them  so i used that strategy put it to work  for my business as well and i started  making partnerships and i started  reaching out to distributors and all  sorts of different companies who are  related to my industry  i found them online i did a google  search i went looking for related  businesses  and i gave them an incentive  most of them were a commission based i  gave them incentive to sell our product  and some people paid in advance  and after  you know a year of struggling and not  being able to make this work within my  first month of china partnership  strategy i landed a deal with a company  in europe who paid me thirteen thousand  dollars  as a fee to be our exclusive partner for  certain markets in europe  thirteen thousand dollars  now that may not be a lot to you guys  right now but you know i'm making 300  bucks a month that's what i'm pulling  out